events.description:
TVS Club meetings are open to all members and the public.&nbsp;See TVS newsletter www.trivalleystargazers.org&nbsp;for details on how to participate in the zoom video conference call.
&nbsp;
Zoom link: https://us02web.zoom.us/j/84110975089?pwd=9iCSFNBwQbq4gldKK6wkaabbpJkOT7.1#success

We have scheduled a club/public star party at the Del Valle Arroyo Rd Staging area for Saturday November 22. Setup starts about 4:45. The public portion runs from about 5:30-8:30. Curfew is 10 pm, so if we stick around that long, we have to make sure the public has vacated by then.
&nbsp;
The star party is at the Arroyo Rd Staging area just past 5055 Arroyo Rd. This is not the main entrance to del valle, but rather a gravel lot past the golf course and VA hospital down Arroyo street (an extension of L street).
&nbsp;
Weather permitting, we should have a good view of the moon and the fall objects and Saturn with Jupiter and Orion coming up a bit later. Views to the south are blocked by a large hill, but otherwise is relatively free many of the normal sight blocking objects. The skies are relatively dark for being very close to Livermore.
&nbsp;
I hope to get several club members with telescopes or binoculars. If you don't have a telescope or binoculars to share, please come anyway and enjoy the star party and feel free to stick around after the public leaves. Please let me know if you are bringing your equipment to share. We need several telescopes to make this a successful event.
&nbsp;
Thanks,
Johnathan
&nbsp;
Coordinates: (37.6196638, -121.7528899)
